            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/registry/message_registry.json",
                    "line": 6903,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ramesh Iyyar",
                        "email": "rameshi1@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "RameshIyyar"
                    },
                    "message": "Is it planned to use only for the Active BMC triggered FO is failed?\n\nI think we could use the same error if the FO triggered externally or host also, right?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/registry/message_registry.json",
                    "line": 6903,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "There's already 'Failover Rejected' errors. This one is for when the failover was started but for some  reason didn't actually work.\n\nDid you have another specific case in mind?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/registry/message_registry.json",
                    "line": 6903,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ramesh Iyyar",
                        "email": "rameshi1@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "RameshIyyar"
                    },
                    "message": "Does \"Failover Rejected\" mean that failover is not permitted at that moment?\n\nWhat happens if failover is allowed initially, but the operation fails while processing a failover request from Redfish or the host? Do we need to create error log, right?\n\nIf its already covered then I am fine with this."
                },
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/registry/message_registry.json",
                    "line": 6903,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Matt Spinler",
                        "email": "spinler@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "spinler"
                    },
                    "message": "> Does \"Failover Rejected\" mean that failover is not permitted at that moment?\nYep\n\nAt this point there is no spot for an in progress failover to 'fail', as it immediately resets the original active and then itself takes active.  Then any errors are detected normally, like if redundancy can't be enabled again for some reason."
                },
                {
                    "file": "extensions/openpower-pels/registry/message_registry.json",
                    "line": 6903,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ramesh Iyyar",
                        "email": "rameshi1@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "RameshIyyar"
                    },
                    "message": "OK"
                }
            ],
